  "slug": "codes-topic-f271",
  "summary": "Five preprints use symmetry, code structure, or constraints to reduce Toffoli counts and circuit resources in state preparation, compilation, and magic-state factories.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is circuit construction that exploits explicit structure to reduce resource cost. Two preprints prepare DMRG matrix product states by using spin symmetry: abelian-symmetric block-sparse protocols cut Toffoli counts by up to 135x, and a non-Abelian SU(2) approach uses Wigner-Eckart reduction and Clebsch-Gordan transforms. CSS-T-Product codes, whose transversal phase gates implement multi-qubit logical diagonal gates, enable tailored magic-state factories. A structure-aware compiler with persistent occupancy encoding preserves constraints for independent-set optimization circuits. PP-VarQITE combines Pauli propagation with variational imaginary-time evolution for shallow thermal-state circuits, demonstrated on up to 98 qubits. The items address different circuit classes and do not share a single method; the common element is tying synthesis to symmetry or code structure.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
